# Intent: Overlay readability pass, part 2, the unit side. The overlay engine now has three layers (weather, event, front) in PSRAM; post_to_flush draws them front to back with the banner row and the subtitle strip left alone while they show (the banner zone counts as busy for the row, a chip or any strip glyph: maipai_banner_zone_busy) and with the eyes and the mouth of the style on screen protected (dark pupils and open mouths are not background). When a text zone appears or goes away its rows are invalidated once so they are drawn again with or without the overlays. self.overlay.set takes the ten named combinations (a combination replaces everything, a single overlay replaces its layer and ends a combination), self.overlay.status lists three layers and all the names, and the sleepy look's zzz does not replace a running combination. The tool text lists every name and says what stays on top. The glow is centered on the eye from ml_eye_center_y (the face zone middle, y 106, plus the style's eye offset): it was placed from y 120, the middle of the screen, which N04 stopped using, so it sat 14 px low.
# Placement: unit (the overlays run on the robot with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_look_core.h (ours, patch X01, N04), firmware/main/hal/maipai_fx.cc (ours, patches TA03, TC03, N02), maipai_banner.cc and maipai_banner.h (ours, patches N01, FI01)
# Check after a flash: with a banner message showing, rain or stormy never draws in rows 0 to 27; with a subtitle showing, never in rows 184 to 239; self.overlay.set stormy, rainy, snowy, sunny, windy, night, party, celebrate, love and sleeping each answer {ok:true}; self.overlay.status shows the layers; heap: internal free steady unchanged, PSRAM down by 1.4 KB.

